=== p2-windows · W7 · page:system/StatusApiDocs (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:system/StatusApiDocs   kind=page   web route=/docs/status-api
Web source  : web/src/features/system/pages/StatusApiDocsPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/StatusApiDocsPage/ (+ NavigationView registration, test, ledger)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent
  view), exactly as the sibling W7 HelpPage / DataExportPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "TeslaSync/Features/System/StatusApiDocsPage.xaml + StatusApiDocsPageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto these real
  conventions. The namespace is TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.SystemOps (aligns with RouteGroup.SystemOps, the
  manifest's system/ group; a `.System` sub-namespace would shadow the global System namespace).
- A fourth file, StatusApiDocsPage.Examples.cs, holds ONLY the six verbatim example-response payloads. It is
  generated from the web source via JSON.stringify(example, null, 2) so each disclosure shows the identical JSON a
  self-hosted operator reads on the web docs page (byte-for-byte; the live example keeps the web's escaped
  backslash-n, rendered as two backslashes then 'n'). Pure data → linked into the test project for headless assert.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest declares NO API data sources — the web page is explicit static
  documentation ("Static content — no backend round-trip"; it imports no hook, only react-router Link + lucide
  icons). So there is no generated-client feed and no <Name>.Source.cs; StatusApiDocsPageViewModel projects the
  static six-endpoint catalog through StatusApiDocsProjection with zero HTTP. LoadAsync/RefreshAsync honour the
  page lifecycle (OnLoaded → LoadAsync) by re-projecting synchronously (no fabricated network call).
- One data state (manifest: success): the web page has no fetch/loading/error branch, so the honest native union
  is StatusApiDocsState.Success (the catalog yielded endpoints → overview + endpoint cards + footer) plus a
  defensive StatusApiDocsState.Empty branch (a null/empty catalog → overview + a friendly TsEmptyState + footer,
  never a blank region, ADR-011). The overview and footer panels are always visible.
- Panels (ADR-005), in web source order, mapped to the manifest's three GlassPanel slots:
  · GlassPanel1 = the per-endpoint card (web the reusable <Endpoint> component, instantiated 6×). Each is a
    TsGlassPanel (Mica/glass via the W1 surface tokens) holding a method badge (TsBadge Status=Info, web
    Badge variant="info"), the code path (mono + cyan accent token, web text-cyan-200), an optional query hint
    (muted, web ?{query}), the description, and a TsAccordion ("Example response", web <details>/<summary>)
    revealing the verbatim example JSON in a horizontally-scrollable mono block (web <pre> overflow-x-auto).
  · GlassPanel2 = the overview panel (web the first <GlassPanel>): a Server-glyph "Overview" heading, two prose
    paragraphs (mounting/auth, the "Designed for" integration list) and the amber additive-only note (Code glyph +
    warning token, web text-amber-200/80 with the <Code> icon).
  · GlassPanel3 = the closing muted footer panel (web the last <GlassPanel>).
  No hardcoded colours/typography — DisplayTokens (TsColor*/TsChartSpeedBrush/TsColorWarningBrush/TsRadius* +
  TsTypeFontFamilyMono) drive light/dark/high-contrast from W1.
- Header (web PageContainer title/subtitle/actions): the shared native PageContainer surface (the W3 port of
  web/src/components/layout/PageContainer.tsx) carries the heading-level-1 title + muted subtitle; the actions
  slot hosts a chromeless "Back to System Status" HyperlinkButton (web the ArrowLeft Link to="/system-status")
  whose Click raises NavigationRequested → the shell NavigateTo. The page body is centred at max-width 768
  (web max-w-3xl mx-auto) with 20px section gaps (web space-y-5).
- Navigation entry: RouteTable.cs already maps Page("StatusApiDocs","docs/status-api",RouteGroup.SystemOps,…) —
  unchanged. ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers the page factory
  (new FeatureViews.SystemOps.StatusApiDocsPage(); NavigationRequested → NavigateTo). The back-link target
  (/system-status) is an existing canonical route — this page introduces NO new surface.
- i18n (ADR-014): the web page hardcodes every literal (it has zero useTranslation calls; the manifest extracted 0
  string keys). The platform catalog Strings/en|ar|he/Resources.resw is AUTO-GENERATED from the web i18n source
  ("do not edit by hand") and therefore carries no statusApiDocs.* keys. Per the established HelpPage precedent,
  every visible literal is still externalised through ILocalizer.GetString(key, englishFallback) under a new
  statusApiDocs.* namespace (title/subtitle/back/overview.{title,p1,p2,note}/exampleResponse/footer/empty +
  endpoints.<id>.description). Absent keys resolve to the verbatim web English copy via the fallback (the
  ShellLocalizer → ResourceLoader bridge), so the page is fully localisable yet introduces zero hardcoded UI text
  and requires no hand-edit of the generated catalog. The endpoint method/path/query strings and the JSON example
  payloads are code/data literals (the web renders them as <code>/<pre>, not translatable prose) and live in the
  catalog, matching how HelpPage keeps routes as data.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties names on the page (title), each endpoint card (method + path + description)
  and the example disclosures; decorative glyphs set AccessibilityView=Raw; the endpoint host is a Main landmark;
  the page exposes a Group automation peer; light/dark + high-contrast honoured through the W1 tokens.
- Units (ADR-005/P1-S5): the page documents an API contract and renders no measured quantities, so no unit
  conversion is involved; the example payloads are reproduced verbatim from the web source.

PRE-EXECUTION FINDING (fixed — tightly coupled, build-blocking):
- ShellWindow.xaml.cs is the single NavigationView registration seam this prompt must edit. At HEAD its "Commands"
  page-factory lambda was syntactically unclosed (the `return page; });` was lost in a prior integration merge,
  splicing the next comment straight after `page.ViewHistoryRequested += …`). That C# syntax error fails the
  pass-1 compile, which crashes the WinUI XAML markup compiler (WMC9999 null-ref) and cascades into 84 "unknown
  type" errors — the whole TeslaSync.App project was RED at baseline. Because the page cannot be registered (nor
  the build gate pass) without editing this exact constructor, the coupled one-line fix (restore
  `return page; });` for the Commands lambda) was applied alongside the StatusApiDocs registration. No other
  behaviour changed.

